WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.100
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.300
is an Emmy-
and Grammy-winning comedian

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.734
who stars in the new show
"The Afterparty,"

00:00:06.734 --> 00:00:09.234
which premieres Friday
on Apple TV+.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:11.701
Here is Tiffany Haddish!

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:12.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.367
Oh, making an entrance!

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.701
Come on!
Oh, my -- [ Laughs ]

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.934
Making an entrance.
Come on.

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.300
Only you.
I love you, bud.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.234
Welcome back to the show.
-Mwah, I love you, too, Jimmy.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:28.601
-You know, Tiffany, I was very
excited to have you on the show.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.834
You've been booked for months.

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:32.234
We want to talk about
"The Afterparty."

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:35.534
And I know you had a very public
breakup, and then I just saw

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:39.234
you were on the news last week.
And so I go, "Hey, you know..."

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.000
and hopefully you know this,
"...that I'm your friend."

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.067
So I love you.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:43.367
So you're always welcome
on the show.

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:45.801
But you can always cancel on us,
as well, if you want to.

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:46.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.501
But you were like,
"No, I'm a pro.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:51.367
I'm gonna come on."
So I appreciate you coming on.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.767
I mean, can you --

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.400
-Well, I appreciate you
having me, Jimmy.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.467
Thank you for, you know,
allowing me to be here.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.133
-Can you talk
about anything that happened

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.634
or want to talk about it or no?

00:01:01.634 --> 00:01:04.534
-Well, I can say this, Jimmy.
-Okay.

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:08.400
-I've been praying to God to
send me a new man, a good man.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:13.901
And God went ahead and sent me
four in a uniform.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.734
[ Laughter ]
I wasn't expecting it.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:18.834
Was not expecting that at all.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.834 --> 00:01:21.100
And now,
I got a really great lawyer,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.968
and we're gonna work it out.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:26.400
-And I got to get my --
my asking of things

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.534
to God a little better.

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:28.901
-Yeah, got to be
a little clearer.

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:30.100
[ Laughter ]
That's very good.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.167
I'm very glad
you're here tonight.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:35.300
I understand it was a tough,
tough week for you.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:39.200
I mean, you lost a few people
very close to you.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.634
I'm very sorry about that.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:45.400
I mean, one of our mutual
friends, Bob Saget,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.067
who was, like, a big mentor
to me, a big brother,

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.767
father figure, he --
he meant a lot to me.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:54.868
-Funny, funny, funny dude.
-Funny man.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:58.901
He was the first white man to
ever tell me, "Just be yourself.

00:01:58.901 --> 00:02:00.534
Just be who you are, Tiffany."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.534 --> 00:02:03.400
"Don't worry about nothing.
Just be you."

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.701
-Is that right?
-And that was huge for me.

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.701
And then,
my grandma passed away,

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.200
and that --
She saved my life.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.801
You know, that was --
That's my heart.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:13.601
Like -- she was,
like, my soul mate.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:16.200
-Yeah.
-That's been really hard

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.067
to process all this,
you know, grief.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:19.767
-Yeah.
-The grief.

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.367
-Well, if you were here,
I would --

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.267
I would give you a hug,
and I would say,

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.067
"It only gets better."
You know?

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.834
And these are the tough times,
and you're gonna get

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:30.234
through it, and I love
that you came on our show.

00:02:30.234 --> 00:02:32.634
This is the first step.
I love that you did this.

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.968
I'm, like --
It takes a lot of guts.

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.834
So I appreciate that.
You're awesome, buddy.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:39.968
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:41.501
-We're comedians.
We got to make each other laugh.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:43.934
We got to make people happy.
-Right, right.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:46.267
Well, also, you know,
just being in your presence,

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:49.300
even though it's through Zoom,
it's, like, through the energy,

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.434
it's -- it brings me joy.

00:02:51.434 --> 00:02:52.501
-Good!
-I miss you.

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:53.534
-I miss you, too.

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:55.167
-And this is
how I get to see you.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.467
-Take this --
Take this, maybe,

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.567
and, hopefully, make something
out of it, you know?

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:00.567
-Oh, I'm definitely
making something out of it.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:02.701
My next special
is gonna be about grief.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.534
-It is?
-And it's gonna be hilarious.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.934
-I love that!
I love that you're doing this.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.200
Because figuring out
how to process it,

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.267
you know, process it all --
kids get to cry

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.734
whenever they want to,
wherever they want to.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.534
As an adult, you can't do that.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.267
You can't just
cry at work like that.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:19.501
They send you home.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:20.767
-That's right.
They send you home.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:24.100
-I mean, I need my money.
-They do.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.467
Well, do it.
Make a special

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.100
and win another Grammy,
will you?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.534
Congrats on --
-Oh, I sure will.

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:30.467
-Congratulations on winning
that Grammy, by the way, bud.

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:36.701
-That's -- a Grammy
is a really cool award.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:39.133
Out of all the awards,
that one's, like, cool.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.601
Because you kind of grew up --
-It is. It is.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:42.434
You can drink out of it.
-Yeah, exactly right.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.801
[ Laughter ]
Exactly right.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.934
Yeah, I -- but you,
as a comedian -- I don't know --

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:50.000
you don't even dream about
winning a Grammy.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.234
You think of, like,
Michael Jackson or somebody

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.901
or, you know, Whitney Houston
or somebody

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:55.634
winning all these Grammys.
You don't think that a comedian

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.467
is gonna win one,
and then you have one.

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:59.334
-Never. Never.
I remember the first time

00:03:59.334 --> 00:04:02.601
I was nominated for a Grammy
for my audiobook,

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.934
for reading out loud.
I was like, "What? What?"

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:07.634
Like, "You can get a Grammy
for reading out loud?"

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.000
[ Laughter ]
And I called my drama teacher

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.434
immediately,
my high school drama teacher,

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.834
who taught me how to read.
And I was like,

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.467
"Girl, you did a good job!

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.868
Just got nominated for a Grammy
for reading out loud."

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:20.100
-"I'm a Grammy-nominated
reader."

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.968
"I'm a Grammy-nominated reader."
-Yeah.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:27.067
-I read something funny in one
of your interviews recently.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:31.300
You said that you want to make
80 films by the time you're 50.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.033
-Yes. But I don't want
to be in all of them, okay?

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.934
I just want to make them.

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.767
I want to be
a part of

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.767
the moviemaking process
in some way.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:43.334
80 of them by the time I'm 50.
-Why 80?

00:04:43.334 --> 00:04:46.100
-Because it's a nice,
well-rounded number.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:50.501
And it seems to me that,
you know, if you make 80 films

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:54.501
that, you know, you're --
you're an official entertainer.

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:56.834
You are, like, the thing.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.400
-80 fil--
I love that.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.267
I love that you're doing that.
Because I saw --

00:05:00.267 --> 00:05:02.434
"The Afterparty," by the way,
super funny.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:05.701
Oh, my gosh.
I mean, what a talented cast.

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.767
You sent a couple pictures.
This is you

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.434
as a camera operator
on "The Afterparty."

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.667
-Yeah, yeah. See?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.868
I'm a camera operator already.
-Does this count?

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.601
Does this count as one of the --
-Yes, that counts.

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:20.000
To me, that counts.
You know, I put in an invoice

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.601
for a check
for the camera operator job.

00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:23.834
They didn't pay me for that
part, but I put in an invoice.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:26.234
-How about --
How about boom operator?

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:27.234
-Boom operator.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:28.868
That's why I got
these strong arms.

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.000
You know, bam!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.367
Yeah.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.000
-I want to talk about
"Afterparty," if you can.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.701
Because --
Let's just, how about this?

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:37.834
What was your best after party

00:05:37.834 --> 00:05:40.100
you've ever been to
in your life?

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.501
-Best after party I ever been to
in my life would have to be

00:05:43.501 --> 00:05:47.734
the Jay Z/Beyoncé gold party
after the Oscars.

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:49.400
-Oh!
-That's the best party

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.634
I ever been to, because, first
of all, good music, good food.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.868
And then, there's something
about when you're, like,

00:05:55.868 --> 00:05:58.267
dancing, you know,
eating all some fries

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:01.100
and dancing and you look over,
and there goes Rihanna.

00:06:01.100 --> 00:06:04.167
"Hey, hey, Lupita!
What's up, girl?

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:07.300
Oh, Leonardo!
What's going on, Leonardo?

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.200
We ready!
Hey!"

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.968
Oh, Beyoncé dancing with me.

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.834
Me and Beyoncé dancing.
We getting it, we getting it.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.801
Now, most people
would be intimidated

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:18.634
to dance next to Beyoncé,
but I feel like Beyoncé

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:22.067
is intimidated dancing next to
me, because I got them moves.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.601
Okay? I been killing it
on the dance floor.

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:26.934
Mostly my pinky toe.
-That's crazy.

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.634
-'Cause she got me
some slippers.

00:06:28.634 --> 00:06:30.767
She was like,
"Here you go, girl.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.300
You ain't got no shoes on.
Here you go."

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:33.701
-That's right.
That's fun.

00:06:33.701 --> 00:06:35.868
I want to hear more about
the show and see a clip from it

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.467
when we come back.
More with Tiffany Haddish

00:06:37.467 --> 00:06:39.133
after the break, everybody.
Come on back.

